Prefix: : <https://finsight-tech.com/ontology/examples/business-events#>
Prefix: xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>

Ontology: <https://finsight-tech.com/ontology/examples/business-events>


# ************************************************************************
# Business Events - Financial Occurrences
# ************************************************************************
#
# Models financially meaningful occurrences such as trade execution,
# payment and settlement. The example distinguishes business events from
# notifications, system updates, workflow tasks and resulting states.
#

Datatype: xsd:dateTime

### Core financial concepts

Class: Party

Class: Security

Class: PaymentObligation

Class: SettlementInstruction

Class: Contract


### Business events

Class: BusinessEvent

Class: TradeExecution
    SubClassOf: BusinessEvent

Class: Payment
    SubClassOf: BusinessEvent

Class: Settlement
    SubClassOf: BusinessEvent

Class: AmendmentEvent
    SubClassOf: BusinessEvent


### Event timing

# occurredAt represents the time of the occurrence in this focused example.
# Effective time and system-recorded time may be different and are modelled
# separately when those distinctions matter.

DataProperty: occurredAt
    Domain: BusinessEvent
    Range: xsd:dateTime


### Trade execution relationships

ObjectProperty: hasBuyer
    Domain: TradeExecution
    Range: Party

ObjectProperty: hasSeller
    Domain: TradeExecution
    Range: Party

ObjectProperty: executedSecurity
    Domain: TradeExecution
    Range: Security


### Payment relationships

ObjectProperty: hasPayer
    Domain: Payment
    Range: Party

ObjectProperty: hasPayee
    Domain: Payment
    Range: Party

ObjectProperty: appliedTo
    Domain: Payment
    Range: PaymentObligation


### Settlement relationships

ObjectProperty: settlesInstruction
    Domain: Settlement
    Range: SettlementInstruction


### Amendment relationships

ObjectProperty: amends
    Domain: AmendmentEvent
    Range: Contract


### Focused event semantics

Class: BilateralTradeExecution
    SubClassOf:
        TradeExecution,
        hasBuyer exactly 1 Party,
        hasSeller exactly 1 Party,
        executedSecurity exactly 1 Security

Class: PaymentAgainstObligation
    SubClassOf:
        Payment,
        hasPayer exactly 1 Party,
        hasPayee exactly 1 Party,
        appliedTo exactly 1 PaymentObligation


### Observation and system-recording concepts

# These concepts are intentionally shallow. They are included only to show
# that learning about an occurrence and recording it are not the occurrence
# itself.

Class: SettlementConfirmationReceived

Class: SystemStatusUpdate

ObjectProperty: reportsSettlement
    Domain: SettlementConfirmationReceived
    Range: Settlement

ObjectProperty: recordsSettlement
    Domain: SystemStatusUpdate
    Range: Settlement


### Workflow concepts

# A workflow task describes work to be performed. It is not the same thing
# as the business event that may result from that work.

Class: WorkflowTask

Class: SubmitSettlementInstructionTask
    SubClassOf: WorkflowTask

ObjectProperty: actsOn
    Domain: WorkflowTask
    Range: SettlementInstruction


### Modelling boundaries

# BusinessEvent                  - a financially meaningful occurrence
# SettlementConfirmationReceived - information that a settlement occurred
# SystemStatusUpdate             - a change in a system representation
# WorkflowTask                   - work that should be performed
#
# These concepts are related but should not be collapsed into one event type.
#
# The file also does not model resulting states such as Settled or Satisfied.
# Event-to-state semantics belong to the next modelling problem.